EXPERIMENT 1.1: Contains Duplicate (LC 217)

Aim:
To determine whether an integer array contains any duplicate element using sorting.

Algorithm:
1. Read the input array nums.
2. Sort the array in ascending order.
3. Traverse the sorted array from index 1 to the last element.
4. Compare each element with its previous element.
5. If two consecutive elements are equal, return true.
6. If no duplicate is found after the traversal, return false.

Code:

class Solution {
public:
    bool containsDuplicate(vector<int>& nums) {
        int nums_size = nums.size();

        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        for (int i = 1; i < nums_size; i++) {
            if (nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) {
                return true;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }
};


