EXPERIMENT 1.2: Contains Duplicate II (LC 219)

Aim:
To determine whether an integer array contains duplicate elements such that the difference between their indices is at most k using a hash map.

Algorithm:
1. Read the input array nums and integer k.
2. Create an unordered_map to store each element and its latest index.
3. Traverse the array from index 0 to the last element.
4. If the current element is already present in the map:
   a. Calculate the difference between the current index and the stored index.
   b. If the difference is less than or equal to k, return true.
5. Update the current element's latest index in the map.
6. If no such duplicate is found, return false.

Code:

class Solution {
public:
    bool containsNearbyDuplicate(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        unordered_map<int, int> mpp;
        int n = nums.size();

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (mpp.find(nums[i]) != mpp.end()) {
                if (i - mpp[nums[i]] <= k) {
                    return true;
                }
            }
            mpp[nums[i]] = i;
        }

        return false;
    }
};
